    "exact_path_candidates": [
      {
        "id": "AUDIT-ROW-ASSUMPTIONS-UNRECORDED",
        "title": "Per-function and per-unit audit rows carry no assumptions: declared libc premises and Fluent Bit reachability premises live only in run-level text",
        "why": "MEASURED by card STABILITY-REEVAL-5 (wave-45 close, base 8c1f15eb): the W45 slice's resource-diagnostics.json (docs/reports/w45-fb-retry-lifetime/artifacts/slice-after-providers-046accf6/) has top-level keys diagnostic_counts, enumeration_meaning, fluent_bit_revision, line_coordinates, not_projected_meaning, origin_meaning, reason_code_meaning, schema_version, scope, units, and unit rows carry no assumptions key, although OR-1's provisional Unsafe rests on the synchronous-proxy premise and OR-7's on unchecked neutrality (W45-FB-CROSS-UNIT-USER-PREMISES); unit assumptions are written only for no-build units (crates/qcore-audit/src/report.rs:301-304). The corpus's 22 W43 libc moves to Safe rest on declared, unchecked contracts disclosed at run level only (contracts.json trust string). Hard invariant 2 requires assumptions in every published result. DISCHARGE: each published row (or a linked sidecar keyed by row) names the premises and declared contracts it used, or the verdict contract states that a run-level assumption set suffices and every report says so.",
        "source": "docs/reports/stability-reeval-5/README.md",
        "recorded_by": "STABILITY-REEVAL-5"
      },
      {
        "id": "W45-SR5-PENDING-INVENTORY-ARM-UNDRIVEN",
        "title": "The audit's inventory arm that withholds a Pending unit is driven by no fixture",
        "why": "MEASURED by card W45-SR5-SOUNDNESS: crates/qcore-audit/src/projection.rs now makes a Pending unit Unknown when the enumeration inventory does not support a unit Safe, as it already withheld a Safe one. The audit-route fixture (crates/qcore-audit/tests/sr5_pending_gates.rs) reaches the gateway's unread-definition gate first (its reason names `kr_width`), so this arm, like the Safe arm beside it, turns no test red when deleted. Fail-closed by reading. Size: 1 arm. DISCHARGE: a fixture whose enumeration completeness is refused (an undecided conditional group) beside a held call, asserting the unit Unknown with the inventory's reason.",
        "source": "docs/reports/w45-sr5-soundness/README.md",
        "recorded_by": "W45-SR5-SOUNDNESS"
      }
    ],
    "limitation": "Also inspect affected report follow-ons and semantic topic residuals."
  },
